BT 72 720 Td 14 TL /F1 12 Tf (2 The GraphWeave Benchmark) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (The GraphWeave benchmark suite contains nine synthetic tasks spanning node) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (classification, link prediction, and graph regression. Unlike collections) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (assembled from real-world datasets, GraphWeave tasks are generated from) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (controlled random graph processes, so difficulty can be varied along a single) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (axis at a time. The suite is described here only to provide stable reference) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (points for retrieval evaluation.) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (The most informative probe in the suite is the Weave-Depth protocol, which re-) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (trains the same architecture at increasing depths while holding parameter) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (count constant. Under the Weave-Depth protocol, accuracy retention falls to) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (61.3% beyond twelve layers, even with residual connections and normalization.) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (We refer to this behaviour throughout the survey as depth saturation.) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (3 The Message-Passing Design Space) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (A message-passing layer is determined by three choices: the message function,) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (the aggregation operator, and the update function. Sum aggregation preserves) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (multiset information but couples the representation to node degree; mean) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (aggregation is degree-invariant but lossy; attention-based aggregation learns) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (weighting at the cost of additional parameters.) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (Across GraphWeave tasks, sum aggregation with a two-layer MLP update is the) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (most robust default. Learned edge features help only when the generator) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (injects edge semantics, which confirms that design choices should follow the) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (data-generating process rather than leaderboard fashion.) Tj T* ET
endstream
